1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,420
Here's the solution for the go or no go exercise.

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,525
Let's walk through each feature one by one.

3
00:00:06,525 --> 00:00:10,830
The first feature is real time inventory availability.

4
00:00:10,830 --> 00:00:16,380
The issue with this feature is that returns are not added back to available inventory.

5
00:00:16,380 --> 00:00:20,850
This creates a risk that some items may show as out of stock,

6
00:00:20,850 --> 00:00:22,950
even though they're actually available.

7
00:00:22,950 --> 00:00:26,685
But this doesn't really negatively impact the user experience.

8
00:00:26,685 --> 00:00:29,760
With this issue inventory is under reported.

9
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:34,860
This means that we're confident that if we show you that something is in stock.

10
00:00:34,860 --> 00:00:38,055
It will actually be in stock and on the shelf.

11
00:00:38,055 --> 00:00:39,780
In some cases though,

12
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:44,500
we might say that an item is out of stock even though it's actually not.

13
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:47,750
This feature is still an overall improvement for

14
00:00:47,750 --> 00:00:51,355
users and there's no need for any mitigations.

15
00:00:51,355 --> 00:00:53,605
We should go ahead and launch it.

16
00:00:53,605 --> 00:00:57,380
The second feature is sending your shopping list to a friend.

17
00:00:57,380 --> 00:00:59,915
But there's also an issue with this feature.

18
00:00:59,915 --> 00:01:02,570
The shopping lists can only be sent to users

19
00:01:02,570 --> 00:01:05,585
who already have a grocery store app account.

20
00:01:05,585 --> 00:01:10,370
The risk here is that if the recipient doesn't have a grocery store account.

21
00:01:10,370 --> 00:01:12,620
They won't receive the list even though

22
00:01:12,620 --> 00:01:15,850
the person who sent the list thinks that they will have gotten it.

23
00:01:15,850 --> 00:01:19,085
What can we do to mitigate the risk?

24
00:01:19,085 --> 00:01:22,310
We can only allow users to

25
00:01:22,310 --> 00:01:26,180
share their shopping list with users who have a grocery store account.

26
00:01:26,180 --> 00:01:28,640
This means that when the user enters

27
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:32,255
the email address of the person they want to share their list with.

28
00:01:32,255 --> 00:01:34,070
We need to validate that there's

29
00:01:34,070 --> 00:01:38,315
a grocery store app account associated with that email address.

30
00:01:38,315 --> 00:01:42,200
We should also include additional messaging in the flow,

31
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:46,300
explaining that the recipient must have a grocery store account.

32
00:01:46,300 --> 00:01:50,900
In the future we should consider fixing this and making it better by

33
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:55,880
inviting recipients without an account to sign up when a list is shared with them.

34
00:01:55,880 --> 00:01:58,670
But I don't think that this issue should block

35
00:01:58,670 --> 00:02:01,385
the launch and we should launch this feature.

36
00:02:01,385 --> 00:02:04,685
It makes it easier for users to coordinate shopping.

37
00:02:04,685 --> 00:02:09,920
The next feature is to designate another person to pick up your curbside order.

38
00:02:09,920 --> 00:02:13,830
This feature also has an issue that once the order has been placed,

39
00:02:13,830 --> 00:02:17,840
it's not possible to change the designated pickup person.

40
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:23,135
This creates a risk if users need to change the person who's picking up the order.

41
00:02:23,135 --> 00:02:27,335
However, we don't think that this is something that will happen frequently.

42
00:02:27,335 --> 00:02:30,830
We can mitigate this issue by including messaging in

43
00:02:30,830 --> 00:02:35,210
the checkout flow that the designated pickup person cannot be changed.

44
00:02:35,210 --> 00:02:37,880
We should also brief the support team about

45
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:41,185
this issue in case any users reach out to them.

46
00:02:41,185 --> 00:02:46,115
We should consider if there are any viable temporary workarounds to this issue.

47
00:02:46,115 --> 00:02:51,380
For example, as long as the pickup person has a copy of the email order receipt.

48
00:02:51,380 --> 00:02:53,975
They could be allowed to pick up the order.

49
00:02:53,975 --> 00:02:58,580
We should launch this feature as the risks are not likely to happen often.

50
00:02:58,580 --> 00:03:03,910
We're able to communicate the limitations to users when they place their order.

51
00:03:03,910 --> 00:03:09,740
Next is including a 3D product images on the product details page.

52
00:03:09,740 --> 00:03:13,010
This feature has significantly increased

53
00:03:13,010 --> 00:03:17,385
load times by five seconds when opening a page within the app.

54
00:03:17,385 --> 00:03:22,300
The risk is that this significantly slows down the shopping experience

55
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:27,220
and may cause some users to abandon placing an order altogether.

56
00:03:27,220 --> 00:03:31,980
While this feature does provide a more realistic preview of what products look like.

57
00:03:31,980 --> 00:03:36,085
It doesn't substantially change the shopping experience for users,

58
00:03:36,085 --> 00:03:40,525
but in its current state would actually deteriorate the speed of our app.

59
00:03:40,525 --> 00:03:46,780
We should fix this feature so that load times are more reasonable and then launch it.

60
00:03:46,780 --> 00:03:49,840
But we should not launch it in its current state.

61
00:03:49,840 --> 00:03:55,990
The last feature is to show nutrition and ingredients information for food products.

62
00:03:55,990 --> 00:03:59,290
There is an issue where occasionally the texts

63
00:03:59,290 --> 00:04:02,375
will get truncated when there's lots of ingredients.

64
00:04:02,375 --> 00:04:05,155
This causes the app to feel broken.

65
00:04:05,155 --> 00:04:09,905
Since this is not a critical feature that needs to be launched by a specific time.

66
00:04:09,905 --> 00:04:14,315
We should fix the feature so that it works correctly and then launch it.

67
00:04:14,315 --> 00:04:18,060
But we should not launch it in its current state.

